# SendPulse SMTP

Full skill lives in `docs/sendpulse-smtp-skill/` (adjust path if cloned
elsewhere). Read `docs/sendpulse-smtp-skill/SKILL.md` first; load files from
`references/` and `examples/` there as needed.

Non-negotiable rules when generating SendPulse SMTP code:

1. Auth: `POST https://api.sendpulse.com/oauth/access_token` with
   `client_credentials`; cache the Bearer token (~1 h TTL), refresh on 401.
   Credentials from env vars, never hardcoded.
2. Send: `POST /smtp/emails` — the `html` field MUST be Base64-encoded; always
   include a plain `text` part; `to` is an array of `{name?, email}` objects.
3. `from.email` must be a verified sender on a corporate domain (free mailbox
   domains are rejected). The SMTP account must be activated (moderated) first.
4. Store the returned message `id`; status via `GET /smtp/emails/{id}`.
5. Hygiene: check `GET /smtp/unsubscribe/search?email=` before sending; sync
   `GET /smtp/bounces/day` daily and purge hard bounces; mirror app opt-outs via
   `POST /smtp/unsubscribe`.
6. Retry on 429/5xx with exponential backoff; never retry 4xx validation errors.
7. SMTP relay alternative: `smtp-pulse.com:465` (SSL), login/password from
   *SMTP → Settings → General*.
8. Newsletters to subscriber lists = Email Service API (address books +
   campaigns), NOT a loop over `/smtp/emails` — see
   `references/email-service-api.md`.
